title: "[pallet-xcm] fix dry-run storage side-effects leaking into xcm-emulator"

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    Wraps `dry_run_call` and `dry_run_xcm` in a storage transaction that is
    always rolled back, so XCMP queue writes and event resets from the simulated
    execution never escape into the caller's state. Fixes the xcm-emulator bug
    where dry-run outbound messages were delivered by the subsequent
    `process_messages()` call, silently mutating destination-chain state.
    Removes the `reset_ext()` and no-op `execute_with(|| {})` workarounds that
    were papering over this in `emulated-integration-tests-common`.

crates:
- name: pallet-xcm
  bump: patch
- name: emulated-integration-tests-common
  bump: minor
